.TH REHASH 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 17:02:06
.\"@[$]rehash.1C	1.4	08/15/84 17:02:06 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.fi
.SH NAME
rehash \- re-make the hash table of commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rehash
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B rehash
command is internal to the C Shell. Its purpose is to
create a 
.I hash-table
of the available commands (files) named in the 
.I PATH
shell variable.
.PP
The 
.B
rehash
command is invoked automatically at 
.I login
and must be re-invoked each time there is a change in
either the
.I PATH
variable, or the commands (files) located along the 
.I "search path".
.SH SEE ALSO
.I "The C Shell" 
in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
